1:/// The low-level agent loop: stream the model, execute tool calls, append
2:/// results, re-invoke the model until stop.
3:///
4:/// Ported from pi-mono `packages/agent/src/agent-loop.ts`. Kept close to the
5:/// original control flow so future pi fixes port trivially. Deliberate
6:/// divergences from the TypeScript original:
7:///
8:/// - `AgentMessage` is our [Message] union directly; pi's custom-message
9:///   extension point and `convertToLlm` are absent because our messages are
10:///   already LLM-shaped. [TransformContextHook] (pi's `transformContext`) is
11:///   the only rewrite applied before each provider call.
12:/// - Tools are not self-executing here: pi's `AgentTool.execute` is replaced
13:///   by an injected [ToolExecutor] callback, and the provider adapter is an
14:///   injected [StreamFunction], so the loop is fully unit-testable without
15:///   HTTP or a tool registry. Schema validation and argument preparation
16:///   live in the tool registry's executor adapter; the per-tool
17:///   `executionMode` override is honored here when a [Context] tool is an
18:///   [AgentTool].
19:/// - Hooks (`beforeToolCall`/`afterToolCall`/`transformContext`/
20:///   `prepareNextTurn`) and steering/follow-up message queues are config
21:///   fields here, mirroring pi's `AgentLoopConfig`; the stateful `Agent`
22:///   (same directory) wires its queues and public hooks into them. pi's
23:///   `shouldStopAfterTurn` is not ported yet. pi's `convertToLlm` is absent:
24:///   our messages are already LLM-shaped.
25:/// - `AbortSignal` is [CancelToken]; cancellation is also checked *before*
26:///   each provider call and a synthetic aborted message is produced if the
27:///   token is already cancelled, instead of relying solely on the provider
28:///   returning an aborted error event.
29:/// - pi has no `maxTurns` in `AgentLoopConfig`; neither do we. Turns end when
30:///   the model stops calling tools, fails, or is aborted.
31:/// - pi does not consult `isContextOverflow` in the low-level loop (overflow
32:///   handling lives in the session/compaction layer); neither do we. The
33:///   upcoming hooks (`shouldStopAfterTurn`) are the extension point.
