1:/// Auto-compaction loop shared by the CLI [AgentCli] and the Flutter
2:/// [AgentService]. Single source of truth for:
3:///
4:/// - **smol → main fallback**: when the `smol` summarizer fails (rate
5:///   limit, 403, etc.) and points at a different model/endpoint than the
6:///   main chain, retry once with the main stream. If `smol == main`,
7:///   skip the fallback (it would just re-trigger the same 403).
8:/// - **Transient retry**: 5xx HTTP, `connection closed/reset/aborted`,
9:///   `socket exception`, `stream closed` — up to 3 attempts with
10:///   1s/2s backoff. Hard refusals (`usage limit`, `429`, validation,
11:///   auth) fail-fast — retrying burns the same quota twice.
12:/// - **Multi-pass**: when the post-compaction transcript still exceeds
13:///   the window (e.g. 1M-token session landing in a 200k model,
14:///   short-window on-device contexts), retry the whole pass until it
15:///   fits or the per-run pass cap is hit. Each pass re-estimates tokens
16:///   against the freshly shrunken transcript.
17:///
18:/// Hosts inject the host-specific bits (smol resolver, summarizer,
19:/// persistence, progress sink) through the configuration object — there
20:/// is no implicit coupling to `AgentCli` or `AgentService`.
