979:    // round-1): the abort must not merely cancel the IN-FLIGHT pass — it
980:    // must not be answered with a FRESH pass either (an aborted run's
981:    // post-fold, a relief retry after a cancelled relief). The engines
982:    // report cancelled summarizers as failed passes, so the funnel cannot
983:    // see this off the return value; the sticky flag can.
984:    _throwIfUserAborted();
985:    // Backend agent mode (issue #155): bracket the run so the supervisor
986:    // sees why a turn stalled. Pre-flight runs carry the upcoming turn id
987:    // (the following agent_start reuses it). The end frame comes from
988:    // [_AutoCompactorCliHooks.onDone] — every structured-engine terminal
989:    // path fires it, so even a zero-pass run closes the bracket (issue
990:    // #2273). Classic-engine early returns and user cancellation can still
991:    // bypass it. The pass counter increments per pass receipt in [onPass],
992:    // not here.
993:    _hep?.compactionStart();
994:    // User-wired compaction cancellation (issue #1085 M3): a compaction
995:    // can run 15-30 min (pre-flight, mid-run relief, post-run) and the
996:    // run's own token does not exist for two of those windows — Ctrl+C
997:    // used to be a no-op for the whole duration. The token is also
998:    // LINKED to the live run token when one exists (mid-run relief), so
999:    // `_agent.abort()` cancels the in-flight summarizer too. Explicit
1000:    // aborts only: the run idle watchdog is suspended around relief and
1001:    // never cancels through here.
1002:    final abort = CancelTokenSource();
1003:    _activeCompactionAbort = abort;
