167:    // scan joins the index BEFORE this turn's request is composed (the
168:    // stat is metadata-only; a rescan rides `_reloadSkills` verbatim).
169:    // Real user prompts only — auto-continues never rescan mid-turn (I5).
170:    await _checkSkillsFreshness();
171:    // Pre-flight context guard: when the LIVE context already exceeds the
172:    // compaction threshold, compact BEFORE sending the request — a failed
173:    // post-run compaction (quota-limited smol role, provider outage) used to
174:    // leave every request carrying an over-window payload (ctx 240% gauge).
175:    try {
176:      // gh-1729 review: the pre-flight is where the armed E1 one-shot
177:      // pass must ACT (a compaction before the request) — see
178:      // [_maybeAutoCompact]'s `forceE1Pass`.
179:      await _maybeAutoCompact(forceE1Pass: true);
180:    } on CancelledException {
181:      rethrow;
182:    } on Object catch (error) {
183:      // BEST-EFFORT by contract (the lazy boot cap's backstop transplanted
184:      // to the turn): an unexpected throw — broken stdout mid-report, a
185:      // provider quirk escaping the degradation ladder — must not kill
186:      // the turn. The request is still legal (over-trigger is
187:      // under-window by definition here; over-window resumes were capped
188:      // by the local-trim boot valve) and the next turn retries.
