286:      // word. A zero-pass outcome is a terminal receipt too — the exit
287:      // reason (deciding gate + basis/trigger numbers, threaded from the
288:      // engine) states WHY nothing folded, on both surfaces (OQ2): the
289:      // diagnostic lane for post-mortems and a dim row for the user
290:      // (boot-cap defer precedent). The old `passes > 0` guard here
291:      // turned a gate/engine basis divergence into an unbounded silent
292:      // start loop.
293:      final why = reason ?? 'under-trigger basis (no fold ran)';
