255:/// Applies the `compaction:` tuning keys over [base] (the resolved
256:/// forWindow curve, or a host's explicit settings pin) for a model whose
257:/// (conversation) window is [window].
258:///
259:/// Null/empty [tuning] returns [base] IDENTICALLY (same instance) —
260:/// unset config stays byte-for-byte legacy, the same contract
261:/// `resolveBenchCompactionSettings` ships.
262:///
263:/// The ratio converts to the reserve the trigger consumers already read:
264:/// `reserve = window − floor(ratio × window)`. `floor` keeps the line AT
265:/// or BELOW `r × window` — the configured ratio never fires later than
266:/// configured. The degenerate guards mirror
267:/// [CompactionSettings.forWindow] so the pipeline invariants survive any
268:/// override: a reserve over half the window (a ratio below ~0.5) clamps
269:/// to `window ~/ 4`, a keep over the window clamps to `window ~/ 2` — a
270:/// pass must always free tokens. Pure.
271:CompactionSettings applyCompactionTuning(
272:  CompactionSettings base, {
273:  required int window,
274:  CompactionTuning? tuning,
275:}) {
276:  if (tuning == null || tuning.isEmpty) return base;
277:  final ratio = tuning.triggerRatio;
278:  var reserveTokens = ratio != null
279:      ? window - (window * ratio).floor()
280:      : (tuning.reserveTokens ?? base.reserveTokens);
281:  var keepRecentTokens = tuning.keepRecentTokens ?? base.keepRecentTokens;
282:  if (reserveTokens >= window ~/ 2) {
283:    reserveTokens = math.max(128, window ~/ 4);
284:  }
285:  if (keepRecentTokens >= window) {
286:    keepRecentTokens = math.max(256, window ~/ 2);
287:  }
288:  return CompactionSettings(
289:    enabled: base.enabled,
290:    reserveTokens: reserveTokens,
291:    keepRecentTokens: keepRecentTokens,
292:  );
293:}
